%% SkillForge Architecture Diagrams
%% View at https://mermaid.live or via any markdown renderer
%% Multiple diagrams in one file separated by "---" comment blocks

%% ============================================================
%% Diagram 1 — System Architecture (high level)
%% ============================================================

graph TD
    User[Developer] -->|opens .ipynb| NB[(Jupyter Notebook)]

    NB -->|cell errors| Watcher
    Watcher[Watcher Agent<br/>nbclient hook<br/>captures traceback + cell + ctx] -->|error signature| Retriever

    Retriever[Retriever Agent<br/>embedding match] -.lookups.- SkillStore[(Skill Store<br/>YAML+MD files<br/>+ embedding sidecars)]

    Retriever -->|HIT confidence > 0.80| Applier
    Retriever -->|MISS or low confidence| Diagnoser

    Diagnoser[Diagnoser Agent<br/>LLM reasoning<br/>Minimax / Gemini / Claude]
    Diagnoser -->|structured fix| Distiller
    Distiller[Distiller Agent<br/>distill fix into reusable skill]
    Distiller -->|writes new skill| SkillStore
    Distiller -->|fix code| Applier

    Applier[Applier<br/>MCP server<br/>insert_fix_cell]
    Applier -->|inserts fixed cell| NB

    Applier -.exposed via MCP.- External[External Agents<br/>Claude Code · Cursor · etc.]

    SkillStore -.served by.- MCP[MCP Server<br/>apply_skill / list_skills / record_fix]
    MCP -.- External

    classDef agent fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,color:#1e40af
    classDef store fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,color:#92400e
    classDef external fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#6366f1,color:#3730a3

    class Watcher,Retriever,Diagnoser,Distiller,Applier agent
    class SkillStore store
    class External,NB external

%% ============================================================
%% Diagram 2 — FAST PATH vs SLOW PATH sequence
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Developer
    participant W as Watcher
    participant R as Retriever
    participant S as SkillStore
    participant D as Diagnoser (LLM)
    participant Di as Distiller
    participant A as Applier

    rect rgb(254, 243, 199)
        Note over U,A: SLOW PATH — first encounter (~3000 tokens, ~8s)
        U->>W: Cell errors (pandas dtype mismatch)
        W->>R: traceback + cell + 2 prior cells
        R->>S: embed(traceback) · cosine search
        S-->>R: best match: 0.42 (below threshold)
        R->>D: ask LLM for structured fix
        D-->>R: { diagnosis, fix_code, confidence: 0.91 }
        R->>Di: distill fix into reusable skill
        Di->>S: write skills/pandas-dtype-mismatch.md + .npy
        R->>A: apply fix_code
        A->>U: insert fixed cell · cell turns green
    end

    rect rgb(220, 252, 231)
        Note over U,A: FAST PATH — cache hit (~80 tokens, ~200ms)
        U->>W: Cell errors (similar dtype mismatch, different column)
        W->>R: traceback + cell + 2 prior cells
        R->>S: embed(traceback) · cosine search
        S-->>R: best match: pandas-dtype-mismatch · 0.92 (above threshold)
        R->>A: apply skill template (no LLM call)
        A->>U: insert fixed cell · cell turns green
    end

%% ============================================================
%% Diagram 3 — Skill lifecycle state machine
%% ============================================================

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Empty: no fix attempted

    Empty --> Diagnosing: cache MISS
    Empty --> Applying: cache HIT (template ready)

    Diagnosing --> Distilling: LLM returned valid fix
    Diagnosing --> Failed: LLM failed / low confidence

    Distilling --> Library: skill written to disk
    Library --> [*]: ready for future cache hits

    Applying --> Verifying: fix cell inserted + executed
    Verifying --> Library: success (increment times_used)
    Verifying --> Refining: success but partial · update skill
    Verifying --> Failed: fix didn't work

    Refining --> Library
    Failed --> Diagnosing: retry with augmented context (max 2x)

    state Library {
        [*] --> Active
        Active --> Stale: not used in N days
        Stale --> Active: rehit
        Stale --> Pruned: replaced by better skill (V2)
    }

